MODELS
------

Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2 (speech-to-text, the default)
  NVIDIA. https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2
  int8 ONNX export by the sherpa-onnx project (k2-fsa).
  License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Whisper (speech-to-text, the alternative): ggml weights of OpenAI Whisper base.en / small.en
  OpenAI. https://github.com/openai/whisper (weights converted by whisper.cpp)
  License: MIT

Silero VAD (voice activity detection)
  Silero Team. https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
  License: MIT

Speaker diarization models, through speakrs (used once diarization ships, milestone 2)
  pyannote segmentation: pyannote.audio, Hervé Bredin et al. License: MIT
  WeSpeaker speaker embedding and the pyannote "community-1" clustering parameters.
  License: CC-BY-4.0
  Conversions packaged by the speakrs project (avencera). https://github.com/avencera/speakrs

Hosted and local language models are not distributed with Mirona: Jev (TypeSafe), Ollama models,
OpenAI-compatible endpoints and Anthropic are used under each user's own terms and keys.

